<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff">
    <meta name="description" content="Get started with DataDino placeholder JSON data.">
    <title>Docs — DataDino</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>

<body  class="docs-body">
    <%- include('partials/header') %>

        <main class="docs-layout">
            <aside class="docs-sidebar" aria-label="Documentation navigation">
                <details class="docs-group" open>
                    <summary>Intro</summary>
                    <nav class="docs-group__links" aria-label="Intro">
                        <a href="#test">Test</a>
                        <a href="#limiting-resources">Limiting Resources</a>
                        <a href="#delay-responses">Delay Responses</a>
                        <a href="#resources-auth">Resources as Auth User</a>
                        <a href="#ip-address">IP Address</a>
                        <a href="#openapi-spec">OpenAPI Spec</a>
                    </nav>
                </details>

                <details class="docs-group">
                    <summary>Tools</summary>
                    <nav class="docs-group__links" aria-label="Tools">
                        <a href="#tools-search">Search</a>
                        <a href="#tools-pagination">Pagination</a>
                    </nav>
                </details>

                <details class="docs-group">
                    <summary>Dynamic Image</summary>
                    <nav class="docs-group__links" aria-label="Dynamic Image">
                        <a href="#dynamic-image">Image URL</a>
                    </nav>
                </details>

                <details class="docs-group">
                    <summary>Auth</summary>
                    <nav class="docs-group__links" aria-label="Auth">
                        <a href="#auth-login">Login</a>
                        <a href="#auth-user">Current User</a>
                    </nav>
                </details>

                <details class="docs-group">
                    <summary>Products</summary>
                    <nav class="docs-group__links" aria-label="Products">
                        <a href="#products">All Products</a>
                        <a href="#single-product">Single Product</a>
                    </nav>
                </details>
            </aside>

            <div class="docs-content">
                <header class="docs-overview">
                    <h1>DataDino — Docs</h1>
                    <p>
                        Use these examples to fetch JSON data for frontend projects,
                        try common query options, and test API responses.
                    </p>
                </header>

                <section class="docs-section" id="test">
                    <h2>Test</h2>
                    <p>Check that the API is reachable with a simple request.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/test")
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(console.log);</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="limiting-resources">
                    <h2>Limiting Resources</h2>
                    <p>Use limit, skip, and select to control the response size and fields.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/products?limit=10&amp;skip=5&amp;select=title,price");</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="delay-responses">
                    <h2>Delay Responses</h2>
                    <p>Add a delay query parameter to simulate a slower API response.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/products?delay=1000");</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="resources-auth">
                    <h2>Resources as Auth User</h2>
                    <p>Send a bearer token when requesting a protected resource.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/auth/me", {
  headers: { Authorization: "Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN" }
});</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="ip-address">
                    <h2>IP Address</h2>
                    <p>Request the IP information detected by the API.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/ip")
  .then(response => response.json())
  .then(console.log);</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="openapi-spec">
                    <h2>OpenAPI Spec</h2>
                    <p>Fetch the API schema for use with API tools and code generators.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/openapi.json");</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="tools-search">
                    <h2>Search</h2>
                    <p>Search products with a query string.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/products/search?q=phone");</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="tools-pagination">
                    <h2>Pagination</h2>
                    <p>Use skip and limit to request a different page of results.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/products?limit=10&amp;skip=10");</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="dynamic-image">
                    <h2>Dynamic Image</h2>
                    <p>Build a placeholder image URL with the size you need.</p>
                    <pre><code>https://dummyjson.com/image/300x200</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="auth-login">
                    <h2>Login</h2>
                    <p>Send credentials to receive an authentication response.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/auth/login", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({ username: "emilys", password: "emilyspass" })
});</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="auth-user">
                    <h2>Current User</h2>
                    <p>Use the token returned from login to request the current user.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/auth/me", {
  headers: { Authorization: "Bearer YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN" }
});</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="products">
                    <h2>All Products</h2>
                    <p>Fetch the products collection.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/products");</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="docs-section" id="single-product">
                    <h2>Single Product</h2>
                    <p>Replace 1 with the product ID you want to retrieve.</p>
                    <pre><code>fetch("https://dummyjson.com/products/1");</code></pre>
                </section>
            </div>
        </main>

        <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>

</html>